   "speech": "At the same time, during troubled and strange sleep, which interwove life with an almost tangible world of distinct dreams, he several times heard music from whose very first bars he awoke in a state of half-mad trembling. This music was a revelation of harmony such as had never yet arisen anywhere. Its beauty was terrifying in the supernatural power of its concords, capable, it seemed, of turning hell into azure. The perfection of this divinely exultant music, beyond the grasp of consciousness, was — as Gratien Duplay felt with his whole being — the full embodiment of the shadows of that great enchantment with which he went through life, and which was, presumably, the echo of some radiant primal source.",
